.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
node_modules/
*.log
_qr.html
_syntax.py
__pycache__/
_out.txt

_test.html

_check.mjs

# Everything with a leading underscore is a scratch file: patch scripts,
# probes, their generated .html/.js harnesses and their _out.txt reports.
# The convention was only half-enforced by name until a2.50, when a
# `git add -A` swept 300 of them into a commit. Add with -f if one ever
# deserves to be tracked.
_*
diff.txt

# THE HARNESS IS TRACKED (v2.8d). The rule above was written for patch
# scripts - one-off, disposable, 549 of them - and it swallowed the test
# suite with them: `git ls-files "_*"` returned NOTHING against 262 probe
# and check files. Losing this machine would have lost the ability to check
# any claim in CURRENT_STATE.md, which is most of what that file is for.
#
# These patterns are deliberately shaped so a NEW probe is tracked by
# default: name it `_<thing>_probe.py` / `.js` or `_<thing>chk.py` / `.js`
# and it lands in the repo without anyone remembering to say so.
!_verify.py
!_runprobes.py
!_cmpdirs.py
!_pageschk.py
!_diffprobes.py
!_probe.py
!_probe_js.js
!_*_probe.py
!_*_probe.js
!_*_probe2.py
!_*_probe2.js
!_*chk.py
!_*chk.js

# Two patch scripts that happen to end in `_probe.py`. Not harness.
_fix_probe.py
_fix_probe2.py

# The recorded probe OUTPUTS stay out: the `_v*/` before-and-after folders,
# `_*_out.txt` reports, generated harness HTML and version backups. They are
# regenerable from the tracked scripts and the app, which is the point.
_v[0-9]*/
_a2[0-9]*/
_*_out.txt
_*.html
